    "user_request_original": "Design an asymmetric Fabry-Perot narrowband bandpass filter for 1550 nm LiDAR reception. Incident medium is air. Substrate is Fused Silica. Use only Ta2O5 (Gao) (high index) and SiO2 (Lemarchand) (low index) materials. Stack topology: Air | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao)(cavity) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Fused Silica. This is 11 layers total (4 pairs on input side, 6 pairs on substrate side, plus one cavity layer). Optimize all individual layer thicknesses in nanometers. Target wavelength is 1550 nm at normal incidence. Maximize transmittance at 1550 nm with soft target ≥0.95. Minimize transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm bands. Total layers must not exceed 30.",
